      <p>Waninger v. Marathon Engineering appears to be the first employment-discrimination case in which an AI meeting transcript serves as the plaintiff's primary evidence. No prior case of this type was identified in research — though the absence of evidence is not definitive. The case arrives amid a broader wave of privacy litigation against notetaker vendors, but it belongs to a different category entirely. In the vendor suits, the notetaker is the defendant's product. In Waninger, it is the plaintiff's witness.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="s04">
      <h2><span class="num">04 — SIGNAL</span>The Bind</h2>
      <p>The design behavior being sued as a privacy violation in four courtrooms is the same design behavior that produced the plaintiff's evidence in a fifth. Auto-join. Auto-distribute. Persist for hours. In the vendor suits, these defaults are the injury. In Waninger, they are the windfall.</p>
      <p>This is the story's central structural observation, and it is worth stating as such: no source explicitly argues this connection. The privacy suits and the discrimination case exist in separate courts, with different parties, under different legal theories. The link is that they are consequences of the same factory settings — documented in the manufacturer's own knowledge base, scored at the highest confidence level by the source material.</p>
      <p>The bind is this: any product change that reduces recording to satisfy the privacy plaintiffs — requiring explicit per-meeting consent, limiting session duration, restricting distribution to the meeting organizer — also eliminates the tool's capacity to serve as an impartial witness. If Fireflies had required opt-in recording, the bot might not have been in the termination call. If it had stopped recording when participants dropped off, it would not have captured the post-departure conversation. If it had sent the transcript only to the bot's owner, Waninger would never have received it.</p>
      <p>The inverse holds equally. Any design that preserves the witnessing function — the bot stays, the bot records everything, the bot distributes to everyone — perpetuates the privacy exposure that four separate lawsuits are trying to stop.</p>
      <p>This is not an AI failure story. The tool did exactly what it was configured to do in every case. In the vendor suits, the design is the complaint. In Waninger, the design is the windfall. The notetaker did one thing. The legal system received it as two opposite things. No settings page resolves this. The archive has told stories about algorithms that discriminated (Amazon's resume screener screened out women). This is a story about an algorithm that witnessed alleged discrimination — and is simultaneously being sued, in other courtrooms, for the very behavior that made the witnessing possible.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="s05">
      <h2><span class="num">05 — CONSEQUENCE</span>The Open Record</h2>
      <p>Before the Waninger transcript could reach a jury, it would need to survive a question no court has answered: whether a non-verbatim AI-generated summary is admissible as evidence.</p>
      <p>Ford & Harrison attorney Mark Saloman, writing on Mondaq, states that "a Frye hearing will be helpful for all parties to assess the reliability of the Fireflies app" and that "a potentially significant issue will be whether a non-verbatim AI-generated summary is admissible in court." The transcript is not a recording. It is a model's interpretation of what was said — filtered through whatever summarization and paraphrasing logic Fireflies applies. The fidelity of the alleged remark to the actual words spoken is itself untested.</p>
      <p>Courts are actively grappling with the evidentiary status of AI-generated materials, though no ruling on meeting transcripts exists. In United States v. Heppner (S.D.N.Y., February 2026), the court declined to extend attorney-client privilege to materials a defendant had prepared using a consumer-grade AI platform. Mayer Brown's June 2026 analysis identifies AI notetaker outputs specifically as creating novel privilege and admissibility questions. The legal terrain is forming, but no court has tested AI meeting transcripts specifically.</p>
      <p>New Jersey is a one-party consent state for recording under the New Jersey Wiretapping and Electronic Surveillance Control Act (N.J.S.A. 2A:156A-2, -3, -4), as confirmed by the Reporters Committee for Freedom of the Press. The recording itself is likely lawful under current New Jersey law if any one participant — or the bot's operator — consented. The legal question in Waninger is not whether the recording was lawful. It is whether the AI's paraphrase of it is admissible.</p>
      <p>No answer has been filed. No Frye hearing has been scheduled. The case is seven days old. What is known: the same default behavior sits in five courtrooms under five different legal theories. In four, it is the injury. In one, it is the remedy. No product update resolves this. The tool records everything or it records nothing. There is no setting for "record only the parts that will help and not the parts that will hurt."</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</StoryLayout>

<script>
(function () {
  const canvas = document.querySelector('.ai-notetaker-termination-transcript-canvas') as HTMLCanvasElement | null;
  if (!canvas) return;
  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
  if (!ctx) return;

  const cs = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
  const bgColor = cs.getPropertyValue('--bg').trim() || '#0d0d0d';
  const storyHex = cs.getPropertyValue('--story').trim() || '#94a3b8';

  function hexToRgb(hex: string): [number, number, number] {
    const m = /^#?([0-9a-f]{2})([0-9a-f]{2})([0-9a-f]{2})$/i.exec(hex);
    if (!m) return [148, 163, 184];
    return [parseInt(m[1], 16), parseInt(m[2], 16), parseInt(m[3], 16)];
  }

  const [sR, sG, sB] = hexToRgb(storyHex);
  const prefersReduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

  function storyA(a: number): string { return `rgba(${sR},${sG},${sB},${Math.max(0, Math.min(1, a))})`; }
  function dimA(a: number): string   { return `rgba(232,232,232,${Math.max(0, Math.min(1, a))})`; }
  function redA(a: number): string   { return `rgba(255,77,77,${Math.max(0, Math.min(1, a))})`; }

  /* ── Phase boundaries (60fps x 16s = 960 frames) ── */
  const P1 = 240;    /* Meeting end       */
  const P2 = 480;    /* Departure end     */
  const P3 = 600;    /* Persistence end   */
  const P4 = 780;    /* Distribution end  */
  const P5 = 900;    /* Hold end          */
  const CYCLE = 960; /* Fade + snap reset */

  /* ── Constants ── */
  const N = 8;
  const RING_INT = 60;
  const RING_SPD = 0.3;
  const RING_MAX = 120;
  const MAX_RINGS = 10;
  const N_AMB = 20;
  const N_SCAT = 6;
  const SIG_DUR = 50;
  const ORBIT_K = 0.25;
  const DRIFT_V = 0.4;
  const EV = 3;
  const VIO = 7;

  /* ── Interfaces ── */
  interface PNode {
    ha: number; orf: number; ang: number; aspd: number;
    x: number; y: number; a: number;
    dep: boolean; dvx: number; dvy: number;
    sigArr: boolean; glow: number; rfl: number; rsc: number;
  }
  interface Ring  { r: number; a: number; on: boolean; }
  interface Sig   { tx: number; ty: number; p: number; on: boolean; arr: boolean; }
  interface Scat  { x: number; y: number; vx: number; vy: number; a: number; on: boolean; }
  interface Amb   { x: number; y: number; vx: number; vy: number; a: number; }

  /* ── State ── */
  let W = 0, H = 0, frame = 0, rafId = 0;
  let cx = 0, cy = 0, gFade = 1;
  const nodes: PNode[] = [];
  const rings: Ring[]  = [];
  const sigs: Sig[]    = [];
  const scats: Scat[]  = [];
  const ambs: Amb[]    = [];

  function oR(): number { return Math.min(W, H) * ORBIT_K; }

  /* ── Init helpers ── */
  function initNodes() {
    nodes.length = 0;
    const or = oR();
    for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
      const base = (i / N) * Math.PI * 2;
      const jit  = Math.sin(i * 7.3) * 0.06;
      const ha   = base + jit;
      const orf  = 0.88 + (Math.sin(i * 4.1 + 2.7) * 0.5 + 0.5) * 0.24;
      const aspd = 0.0018 + (Math.sin(i * 5.9) * 0.5 + 0.5) * 0.0012;
      nodes.push({
        ha, orf, ang: ha, aspd,
        x: cx + Math.cos(ha) * orf * or,
        y: cy + Math.sin(ha) * orf * or,
        a: 0.15, dep: false, dvx: 0, dvy: 0,
        sigArr: false, glow: 0, rfl: 0, rsc: 1,
      });
    }
  }

  function initRings() {
    rings.length = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < MAX_RINGS; i++) rings.push({ r: 0, a: 0, on: false });
  }

  function initSigs() {
    sigs.length = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) sigs.push({ tx: 0, ty: 0, p: 0, on: false, arr: false });
  }

  function initScats() {
    scats.length = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < N_SCAT; i++) scats.push({ x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, a: 0, on: false });
  }

  function initAmbs() {
    ambs.length = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < N_AMB; i++) {
      ambs.push({
        x: Math.random() * (W || 800),
        y: Math.random() * (H || 380),
        vx: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.12,
        vy: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.12,
        a: 0.03 + Math.random() * 0.015,
      });
    }
  }

  function resetState() {
    frame = 0; gFade = 1;
    cx = W / 2; cy = H / 2;
    initNodes(); initRings(); initSigs(); initScats();
    if (ambs.length === 0) initAmbs();
  }

  function spawnRing() {
    for (const r of rings) {
      if (!r.on) { r.r = 6; r.a = 0.3; r.on = true; return; }
    }
  }

  function ph(f: number): number {
    if (f < P1) return 0;
    if (f < P2) return 1;
    if (f < P3) return 2;
    if (f < P4) return 3;
    if (f < P5) return 4;
    return 5;
  }

  /* ── Update ── */
  function update() {
    const p = ph(frame);

    /* Rings — CONSTANT TEMPO: the recorder is indifferent */
    if (frame % RING_INT === 0) spawnRing();
    for (const r of rings) {
      if (!r.on) continue;
      r.r += RING_SPD;
      r.a = 0.3 * Math.max(0, 1 - r.r / RING_MAX);
      if (r.a <= 0) r.on = false;
    }

    /* Ambients */
    for (const a of ambs) {
      a.x += a.vx; a.y += a.vy;
      if (a.x < 0) a.x += W; if (a.x > W) a.x -= W;
      if (a.y < 0) a.y += H; if (a.y > H) a.y -= H;
    }

    const or = oR();

    if (p === 0) {
      /* Meeting: nodes orbit loosely */
      for (const n of nodes) {
        n.ang += n.aspd;
        n.x = cx + Math.cos(n.ang) * n.orf * or;
        n.y = cy + Math.sin(n.ang) * n.orf * or;
        n.a = 0.12 + 0.04 * Math.sin(frame * 0.03 + n.ha * 2);
      }

    } else if (p === 1) {
      /* Departure: one node fades every 30 frames */
      for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
        const n = nodes[i];
        const depF = P1 + i * 30;
        if (!n.dep && frame >= depF) {
          n.dep = true;
          const dx = n.x - cx, dy = n.y - cy;
          const d = Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy) || 1;
          n.dvx = (dx / d) * DRIFT_V;
          n.dvy = (dy / d) * DRIFT_V;
        }
        if (n.dep) {
          n.x += n.dvx; n.y += n.dvy;
          n.a += (0.04 - n.a) * 0.04;
        } else {
          n.ang += n.aspd;
          n.x = cx + Math.cos(n.ang) * n.orf * or;
          n.y = cy + Math.sin(n.ang) * n.orf * or;
          n.a = 0.12 + 0.04 * Math.sin(frame * 0.03 + n.ha * 2);
        }
      }

    } else if (p === 2) {
      /* Persistence: center alone, ghosts drifting slowly */
      for (const n of nodes) {
        n.x += n.dvx * 0.15; n.y += n.dvy * 0.15;
        n.a += (0.04 - n.a) * 0.02;
      }

    } else if (p === 3) {
      /* Distribution: signal burst */
      const df = frame - P3;

      if (df === 0) {
        for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
          const hx = cx + Math.cos(nodes[i].ha) * nodes[i].orf * or;
          const hy = cy + Math.sin(nodes[i].ha) * nodes[i].orf * or;
          sigs[i].tx = hx; sigs[i].ty = hy;
          sigs[i].p = 0; sigs[i].on = true; sigs[i].arr = false;
        }
      }

      /* All signals arrive simultaneously */
      const sp = Math.min(1, df / SIG_DUR);
      for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
        const s = sigs[i];
        if (!s.on) continue;
        s.p = sp;
        if (sp >= 1 && !s.arr) {
          s.arr = true; s.on = false;
          nodes[i].sigArr = true;
          if (i === EV) {
            nodes[i].glow = 0.8;
          } else if (i === VIO) {
            nodes[i].rfl = 0.7;
            const hx = s.tx, hy = s.ty;
            for (let j = 0; j < 5 && j < scats.length; j++) {
              const ang = (j / 5) * Math.PI * 2 + Math.sin(j * 3.7) * 0.4;
              const spd = 0.5 + Math.abs(Math.sin(j * 2.3)) * 0.8;
              scats[j].x = hx; scats[j].y = hy;
              scats[j].vx = Math.cos(ang) * spd;
              scats[j].vy = Math.sin(ang) * spd;
              scats[j].a = 0.6; scats[j].on = true;
            }
          } else {
            nodes[i].glow = 0.1;
          }
        }
      }

      for (const sc of scats) {
        if (!sc.on) continue;
        sc.x += sc.vx; sc.y += sc.vy;
        sc.a = Math.max(0, sc.a - 0.008);
        if (sc.a <= 0) sc.on = false;
      }

      if (nodes[EV].sigArr) {
        nodes[EV].rsc = Math.min(1.5, nodes[EV].rsc + 0.017);
      }
      for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
        if (i === EV || i === VIO) continue;
        if (nodes[i].glow > 0) nodes[i].glow = Math.max(0, nodes[i].glow - 0.004);
      }

    } else if (p === 4) {
      /* Hold: evidence steady, violation pulses twice */
      const hf = frame - P4;

      nodes[EV].glow = 0.8;

      const vn = nodes[VIO];
      if (hf < 30) {
        vn.rfl = 0.5 * Math.sin((hf / 30) * Math.PI);
      } else if (hf < 45) {
        vn.rfl = 0;
      } else if (hf < 75) {
        vn.rfl = 0.3 * Math.sin(((hf - 45) / 30) * Math.PI);
      } else {
        vn.rfl = Math.max(0, vn.rfl - 0.015);
      }

      for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
        if (i === EV || i === VIO) continue;
        nodes[i].glow = Math.max(0, nodes[i].glow - 0.003);
      }

      for (const sc of scats) {
        if (!sc.on) continue;
        sc.x += sc.vx * 0.3; sc.y += sc.vy * 0.3;
        sc.a = Math.max(0, sc.a - 0.01);
        if (sc.a <= 0) sc.on = false;
      }

    } else {
      /* Fade */
      gFade = Math.max(0, 1 - (frame - P5) / (CYCLE - P5));
    }
  }

  /* ── Draw ── */
  function draw() {
    ctx!.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    ctx!.fillStyle = bgColor;
    ctx!.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);

    const gf = gFade;
    const or = oR();
    const p = ph(frame);

    /* Ambients */
    for (const a of ambs) {
      if (a.a * gf < 0.003) continue;
      ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.arc(a.x, a.y, 1.5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.fillStyle = dimA(a.a * gf); ctx!.fill();
    }

    /* Signal lines */
    if (p === 3 || p === 4) {
      for (const s of sigs) {
        if (s.p <= 0) continue;
        const dx = s.tx - cx, dy = s.ty - cy;
        const ex = cx + dx * s.p, ey = cy + dy * s.p;
        const la = s.on ? 0.5 : Math.max(0.04, 0.4 - (frame - P3 - SIG_DUR) * 0.002);
        if (la * gf < 0.003) continue;
        ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.moveTo(cx, cy); ctx!.lineTo(ex, ey);
        ctx!.strokeStyle = storyA(la * gf); ctx!.lineWidth = 0.8; ctx!.stroke();
      }
    }

    /* Ghost nodes at drift positions */
    for (const n of nodes) {
      if (n.a * gf < 0.003) continue;
      ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.arc(n.x, n.y, 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.fillStyle = dimA(n.a * gf); ctx!.fill();
    }

    /* Reaction effects at HOME positions */
    for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
      const n = nodes[i];
      if (!n.sigArr) continue;
      const hx = cx + Math.cos(n.ha) * n.orf * or;
      const hy = cy + Math.sin(n.ha) * n.orf * or;

      if (i === EV && n.glow > 0.01) {
        const evR = 4 * n.rsc;
        const gr = ctx!.createRadialGradient(hx, hy, 0, hx, hy, evR * 4);
        gr.addColorStop(0, storyA(n.glow * 0.5 * gf));
        gr.addColorStop(1, storyA(0));
        ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.arc(hx, hy, evR * 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx!.fillStyle = gr; ctx!.fill();
        ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.arc(hx, hy, evR, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx!.fillStyle = storyA(n.glow * gf); ctx!.fill();
      }

      if (i === VIO && n.rfl > 0.01) {
        const rg = ctx!.createRadialGradient(hx, hy, 0, hx, hy, 20);
        rg.addColorStop(0, redA(n.rfl * 0.4 * gf));
        rg.addColorStop(1, redA(0));
        ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.arc(hx, hy, 20, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx!.fillStyle = rg; ctx!.fill();
        ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.arc(hx, hy, 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx!.fillStyle = redA(n.rfl * gf); ctx!.fill();
      }

      if (i !== EV && i !== VIO && n.glow > 0.01) {
        ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.arc(hx, hy, 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx!.fillStyle = dimA(n.glow * gf); ctx!.fill();
      }
    }

    /* Scatter particles */
    for (const sc of scats) {
      if (!sc.on || sc.a * gf < 0.003) continue;
      ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.arc(sc.x, sc.y, 2, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.fillStyle = redA(sc.a * gf); ctx!.fill();
    }

    /* Central node — ALWAYS the same visual. The indifference is the thesis. */
    const cr = 6;
    const cGlow = ctx!.createRadialGradient(cx, cy, 0, cx, cy, cr * 4);
    cGlow.addColorStop(0, storyA(0.35 * gf));
    cGlow.addColorStop(0.5, storyA(0.1 * gf));
    cGlow.addColorStop(1, storyA(0));
    ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.arc(cx, cy, cr * 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx!.fillStyle = cGlow; ctx!.fill();
    ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.arc(cx, cy, cr, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx!.fillStyle = storyA(0.9 * gf); ctx!.fill();

    /* Pulse rings — on top */
    for (const r of rings) {
      if (!r.on || r.a * gf < 0.003) continue;
      ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.arc(cx, cy, r.r, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.strokeStyle = storyA(r.a * gf); ctx!.lineWidth = 0.8; ctx!.stroke();
    }
  }

  /* ── Static frame (reduced motion) ── */
  function drawStatic() {
    ctx!.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    ctx!.fillStyle = bgColor; ctx!.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);
    cx = W / 2; cy = H / 2;
    const or = oR();

    for (let i = 0; i < N_AMB; i++) {
      const ax = W * (0.08 + 0.84 * ((i * 7 + 3) % N_AMB) / N_AMB);
      const ay = H * (0.08 + 0.84 * ((i * 11 + 5) % N_AMB) / N_AMB);
      ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.arc(ax, ay, 1.5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.fillStyle = dimA(0.04); ctx!.fill();
    }

    for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
      const ang = (i / N) * Math.PI * 2;
      const rf  = 0.88 + (Math.sin(i * 4.1 + 2.7) * 0.5 + 0.5) * 0.24;
      const hx  = cx + Math.cos(ang) * rf * or;
      const hy  = cy + Math.sin(ang) * rf * or;
      ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.moveTo(cx, cy); ctx!.lineTo(hx, hy);
      ctx!.strokeStyle = storyA(0.06); ctx!.lineWidth = 0.5; ctx!.stroke();
      ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.arc(hx, hy, 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.fillStyle = dimA(0.08); ctx!.fill();
    }

    const cg = ctx!.createRadialGradient(cx, cy, 0, cx, cy, 24);
    cg.addColorStop(0, storyA(0.35)); cg.addColorStop(0.5, storyA(0.1)); cg.addColorStop(1, storyA(0));
    ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.arc(cx, cy, 24, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx!.fillStyle = cg; ctx!.fill();
    ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.arc(cx, cy, 6, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx!.fillStyle = storyA(0.9); ctx!.fill();

    ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.arc(cx, cy, 35, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx!.strokeStyle = storyA(0.15); ctx!.lineWidth = 0.8; ctx!.stroke();
    ctx!.beginPath(); ctx!.arc(cx, cy, 70, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx!.strokeStyle = storyA(0.07); ctx!.lineWidth = 0.8; ctx!.stroke();
  }

  /* ── Loop ── */
  function tick() {
    frame++;
    if (frame >= CYCLE) resetState();
    update(); draw();
    rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
  }

  /* ── Resize ── */
  const ro = new ResizeObserver(() => {
    const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;
    W = canvas!.offsetWidth; H = canvas!.offsetHeight;
    canvas!.width = W * dpr; canvas!.height = H * dpr;
    ctx!.scale(dpr, dpr);
    cx = W / 2; cy = H / 2;
    if (prefersReduced) drawStatic();
  });
  ro.observe(canvas);

  /* ── Initial setup ── */
  const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;
  W = canvas.offsetWidth; H = canvas.offsetHeight;
  canvas.width = W * dpr; canvas.height = H * dpr;
  ctx.scale(dpr, dpr);

  if (prefersReduced) {
    drawStatic();
    window.addEventListener('pagehide', () => { ro.disconnect(); });
  } else {
    resetState();
    const io = new IntersectionObserver(([e]) => {
      if (e.isIntersecting) { if (!rafId) rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick); }
      else { cancelAnimationFrame(rafId); rafId = 0; }
    }, { threshold: 0.01 });
    io.observe(canvas);
    window.addEventListener('pagehide', () => {
      cancelAnimationFrame(rafId);
      io.disconnect();
      ro.disconnect();
    });
  }
})();
</script>
